<p class="intro">This Isomo Laptop Release Contract (the "Contract") is made between Isomo ("Isomo") and the scholar named in the identification record in this Contract (the "Scholar"). It records the continuation of the existing loan of the laptop, charger, and any issued accessories identified in this Contract. In consideration of Isomo permitting the Scholar to continue using the equipment, the parties agree as follows.</p>
<p class="term"><strong>1. Ownership and loan period.</strong> The equipment remains the sole property of Isomo. This Contract continues a loan and does not transfer ownership. The Scholar may keep and use the equipment through the Scholar's transition to university. At that transition, Isomo will give the Scholar written instructions requiring either return of the equipment or continuation of the loan. Until those written instructions are issued and completed, this Contract remains in effect.</p>
<p class="term"><strong>2. Permitted use, care, and security.</strong> The Scholar shall use the equipment for learning, college preparation, communication, Isomo activities, and other lawful educational purposes. The Scholar shall take reasonable care to protect it from theft, water, heat, dust, falls, and rough handling and shall keep it secure when not in use. Without written permission from Isomo, the Scholar shall not install pirated or harmful software, bypass Isomo security, remove managed accounts, factory-reset the laptop, open its casing, remove Isomo labels, replace parts, or sell, pledge, lend, transfer, or otherwise give possession of the equipment to another person.</p>
<p class="term"><strong>3. Reporting and condition record.</strong> The Scholar shall promptly report loss, theft, damage, malfunction, or a missing charger to Pacifique Micomyiza, Bridge2Rwanda Gikondo offices, pmicomyiza@bridge2rwanda.org, 0782555218. The device condition recorded in this Contract documents existing damage or problems disclosed at signing.</p>
<p class="term"><strong>4. Responsibility for loss or damage.</strong> The Scholar is not responsible for normal wear arising from careful use. If Isomo documents that loss or damage resulted from the Scholar's negligence, misuse, or failure to comply with this Contract, the Scholar may be required to pay reasonable repair or replacement costs. Any such responsibility must be based on the documented circumstances and the reasonable cost of repair or replacement.</p>
